Verse 1:
[Eb]There is a [Bb7]land of [Eb]pure [Ab]de[Bb]light,
[Bb7]Where [Eb]bliss [Ab]e[Eb]ter[Bb7]nal [Eb]reigns,
[Eb]Infinite [Ab]day ex[Eb]cludes [Ab]the [Bb]night
[Bb7]And [Cm]plea[C]sures [Eb]ban[Bb7]ish [Eb]pain.
[Eb]We’re trav’[Bb7]ling [Eb]to Im[Ab]manuel’s land,
We [Bb]soon shall hear the trum[Cm7]pet [Bb]sound,
And [Eb]soon we [Bb7]shall with [Eb]Je[Ab]sus [Bb]reign,
[Bb7]And [Eb]never, [Ab]never [Eb]part [Bb7]ag[Eb]ain.
[Eb]What! Never part again? No, [Ab]never part a[Fm]gain,
[Bb7]What! Never part again? No, never part again,
[Cm]And [Eb]soon we [Ab]shall with [Eb]Je[Ab]sus [Bb]reign,
[Bb7]And [Eb]never, [Ab]never [Eb]part [Bb7]ag[Eb]ain.

